## Sprint 2 Goals and Backlog

The goal of Sprint 2 was to start building the basic structure of the Digital Baby Book application.

- Review and improve the wireframes
- Organize the database entities and relationships
- Create the basic project folders and files
- Begin designing the home page
- Begin creating the child profile page
- Upload all new work to GitHub

## What went well this sprint?

I was able to complete the main tasks I planned for this sprint. I created a basic home page and child profile page, organized the database entities and relationships, and uploaded my work to GitHub. I also reviewed the wireframe and made sure the main screens were included.

## What did not go well for this sprint?

I started some of the work later than I planned, so the sprint felt a little rushed. Because of that, I focused more on getting the basic structure completed instead of adding a lot of design or extra features.

## Did you complete the tasks you planned to complete?

Yes, I completed the tasks I planned for this sprint. I created the basic project files, started the home page and child profile page, organized the database design, reviewed the wireframe, and uploaded the new work to GitHub.

## Did you experience any unforeseen technical issues that prevented your progress?

I did not have any major technical issues that stopped me from completing the sprint. The main challenge was making sure I understood what files I needed and how everything should be organized in GitHub.

## Do you feel you are on track to complete your project?

Yes, I feel like I am on track. I now have the basic structure of the project started, and I can continue building on it during the next sprint.

